# cost: the divergence of a ?: in an arm of a branch, and of a ?: in a
# loop body.  A ?: in an arm of a branch runs only for the lanes that
# take that arm, so its warps are counted over those lanes and its
# choice weighed by how many warps get there; one in a loop body is
# counted at every iteration, over the lanes that run it.
#
# warps of 32 consecutive i: the outer condition holds for whole warps
# (a branch); the inner one is reached by a quarter of the warps, and on
# their lanes it never holds
nest(i: u32 in 0..4095) = (i >> 5) % 4 == 0 ? ((i >> 5) % 4 == 1 ? i * i * i * i * i : i + 1) : i * 3
cost nest consecutive i
# the same inner condition where every lane gets to it: a quarter of the
# warps take its first arm
flat(i: u32 in 0..4095) = (i >> 5) % 4 == 1 ? i * i * i * i * i : i + 1
cost flat consecutive i
# a ?: in a loop body whose condition changes with the iteration but not
# within an aligned warp: at each iteration the whole warp takes one arm
lp(i: u32 in 0..1023) = { s: u32 = i; for j in 0..15 { s = ((i >> 5) + j) % 2 == 0 ? s * s * s * 7 : s + j }; s }
cost lp consecutive i
# the lanes independent: at each iteration half of them take each arm
cost lp
